ABOUT THE JOB

In this Client Business Partner role, you will be responsible for the relationship of NielsenIQ’s Strategic Analytics & Insights (SA&I) business with local clients in the Baltics, fostering profitable revenue, and increasing awareness of the broader SA&I portfolio.

RESPONSIBILITIES

• Independently sell Strategic Analytics & Insights solutions, successfully assess the needs of our clients and proactively offer solutions in order to achieve sales targets and maintain a long-term growth focus;
• Developing business with new Clients: identifying needs, building relations, building awareness of research solutions, preparing proposals, negotiating;
• Partnering with local Account Development team to understand client needs and priorities (joint business planning);
• Scope projects responsibly to meet SA&I sales targets and ensure feasibility by partnering with the Solution expert, Customer Success and Operations teams;
• Building SA&I portfolio awareness in and outside of the organisation: presenting at conferences, clients and internal events;
• Participate in the preparation of sales plans and budgets and manage pipeline;
• The person will be responsible for the sales target.

REQUIREMENTS

• 2+ years of experience in market data analyses, research and/or in other marketing services sales;
• Eager to continuously work on further professional development and adoption of technical knowledge related to NIQ tools and services;
• Minimum basic knowledge of consumer and shopper research methodologies;
• Bachelor's Degree required;
• Strong communication skills: verbal and written;
• Ability to build strong relations with Clients, including client management, sales and negotiations;
• High say-do ratio;
• Proficiency in English and one of the local Baltic languages.
• Advantages of experience in working with FMCG or/and Retail;

WHAT WE OFFER

• Annual salary range (including sales package) is between 30.000 - 42.000 EUR. (Offers are made within the disclosed range based on objective, role-related criteria and internal pay equity);
• Hybrid work approach;
• Private Health Insurance compensation package (after the probation period);
• Work in a stable environment, in a large international research company;
• Access to learning platforms, mentorship programs and educational support to keep developing your skills;
• Opportunity to develop within expert groups in various products, methodologies and analytical tools (unique NIQ AI capabilities, AR, Immersive Reality and many more);
• Working in a multi-country environment (on local and multicounty projects).

#LI-Hybrid

Our Benefits

• Flexible working environment
• Volunteer time off
• LinkedIn Learning
• Employee-Assistance-Program (EAP)

NIQ may utilize artificial intelligence (AI) tools at various stages of the recruitment process, including résumé screening, candidate assessments, interview scheduling, job matching, communication support, and certain administrative tasks that help streamline workflows. These tools are intended to improve efficiency and support fair and consistent evaluation based on job-related criteria. All use of AI is governed by NIQ’s principles of fairness, transparency, human oversight, and inclusion. Final hiring decisions are made exclusively by humans. NIQ regularly reviews its AI tools to help mitigate bias and ensure compliance with applicable laws and regulations. If you have questions, require accommodations, or wish to request human review were permitted by law, please contact your local HR representative. For more information, please visit NIQ’s AI Safety Policies and Guiding Principles: https://nielseniq.com/global/en/info/niqs-ai-safety-policies/

About NIQ

NIQ is the world’s leading consumer intelligence company, delivering the most complete understanding of consumer buying behavior and revealing new pathways to growth. In 2023, NIQ combined with GfK, bringing together the two industry leaders with unparalleled global reach. With a holistic retail read and the most comprehensive consumer insights—delivered with advanced analytics through state-of-the-art platforms—NIQ delivers the Full View™. NIQ is an Advent International portfolio company with operations in 100+ markets, covering more than 90% of the world’s population.

For more information, visit NIQ.com

Want to keep up with our latest updates?

Follow us on: LinkedIn | Instagram | Twitter | Facebook

Our commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion

At NIQ, we are steadfast in our commitment to fostering an inclusive workplace that mirrors the rich diversity of the communities and markets we serve. We believe that embracing a wide range of perspectives drives innovation and excellence.  All employment decisions at NIQ are made without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, or gender identity), national origin, age, disability, genetic information, marital status, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable laws. We invite individuals who share our dedication to inclusivity and equity to join us in making a meaningful impact. To learn more about our ongoing efforts in diversity and inclusion, please visit the https://nielseniq.com/global/en/news-center/diversity-inclusion

Als Fysisch Laborant houd je je bezig met de voorbewerking en analyse van verschillende milieumonsters. Je werkzaamheden bestaan onder andere uit:

• Voorbewerken van monsters, zoals ontsluiten, spoelen, drogen, malen en zeven;
• Uitvoeren van fysische bepalingen, waaronder lutum-, organische-stof- en korrelgroottebepalingen;
• Werken met verschillende laboratoriumapparatuur en technieken volgens vaste werkinstructies;
• Beoordelen van werkzaamheden aan de hand van protocollen en voorschriften;
• Signaleren van afwijkingen en storingen en waar nodig actie ondernemen;
• Bijdragen aan een veilige, nette en efficiënte werkomgeving.

Tijdens de nachtdienst

In de nachtdienst werk je zelfstandiger en ben je verantwoordelijk voor de continuïteit van het laboratoriumproces. Je bewaakt de geautomatiseerde processen, signaleert en verhelpt waar mogelijk afwijkingen en voert zelfstandig spoedanalyses uit die gedurende de nacht binnenkomen.

Hierbij zorg je dat urgente monsters tijdig en volgens de geldende kwaliteitsrichtlijnen worden verwerkt en dat de overige processen goed blijven doorlopen.

Je werkt volgens het volgende ploegenschema:

• Ochtenddienst: 07:00 tot 15:30 uur
• Middagdienst: 15:00 tot 23:30 uur
• Nachtdienst: 23:00 tot 07:30 uur

Je werkt nauwkeurig, neemt verantwoordelijkheid en vindt het prettig om zowel zelfstandig als samen met collega's te werken. Ook wanneer je zelfstandig een nachtdienst draait, weet je prioriteiten te stellen en houd je overzicht.

Je hebt:

• Een afgeronde laboratoriumopleiding, bijvoorbeeld MLO niveau 3 of 4;
• Affiniteit met fysische laboratoriumtechnieken;
• Een nauwkeurige en praktische instelling;
• Het vermogen om zelfstandig en geconcentreerd te werken;
• Oog voor kwaliteit en veiligheid;
• Een goede beheersing van de Nederlandse taal;
• De bereidheid om in een 3-ploegendienst te werken.

Je komt terecht in een professionele laboratoriumomgeving met deskundige en betrokken collega's. Je krijgt de ruimte om nieuwe werkzaamheden en technieken te leren en jezelf verder te ontwikkelen.

Daarnaast bieden wij:

• een marktconform salaris passend bij jouw kennis en ervaring;
• een aantrekkelijke ploegentoeslag voor het werken in de 3-ploegendienst;
• een fulltime functie van 39 uur per week;
• minimaal 25 vakantiedagen;
• reiskostenvergoeding, waarbij reizen met het OV 100% wordt vergoed via een NS-Business Card;
• de mogelijkheid om extra gewerkte uren te sparen als tijd voor tijd;
• gratis toegang tot GoodHabitz met een breed aanbod aan trainingen en cursussen;
• volop leer-, ontwikkel- en doorgroeimogelijkheden binnen Eurofins.

Interesse?

Wil jij bijdragen aan betrouwbare milieuanalyses en zoek je een functie waarin laboratoriumwerk, techniek en zelfstandigheid samenkomen? Dan maken we graag kennis met je.

Solliciteer via de sollicitatiebutton en stuur ons jouw cv en motivatie.

Acquisitie naar aanleiding van deze vacature wordt niet op prijs gesteld.

Over Eurofins

Eurofins Scientific is een internationaal life sciences bedrijf dat klanten ondersteunt met laboratoriumonderzoek en advies. De geaccrediteerde laboratoria van Eurofins Milieu voeren in Nederland een breed pakket aan chemische, fysische en biologische analyses uit.

Onze opdrachtgevers zijn onder andere overheden, waterkwaliteitsbeheerders, milieuadviesbureaus en bedrijven. Binnen Eurofins Milieu werken circa 700 collega's aan het traject van monstername tot digitale rapportage van analyseresultaten. Een groot deel van de analyses wordt uitgevoerd in onze laboratoria in Amsterdam en Amersfoort

Front Office Supervisor

You are outgoing and love meeting new people from all over the world. You are focused and driven to make each guest’s experience unique, while also creating a positive atmosphere within the Front Office team. In other words, you are the perfect Front Office Supervisor!

A Day as a Front Office Supervisor at Novotel

As a Front Office Supervisor, you are responsible for the daily operations of the Front Office department. You are the first point of contact for our guests, assisting them with requests and resolving complaints in a professional and creative manner. During your shifts, you help create a positive atmosphere within the Front Office team, consisting of 24 team members. In addition, you are a structured and well-organized leader, ensuring that shifts run smoothly for both yourself and the team. Besides the operational side of the Front Office, you also support various administrative tasks. These may include reviewing and writing emails, preparing staff schedules, conducting job interviews together with HR or the Front Office Manager, and leading performance reviews and training sessions. Of course, we will provide you with the guidance and support you need to succeed in these responsibilities!

Are You the Perfect Reception Supervisor?

Novotel Amsterdam City is looking for someone who:

• Has at least 2 years of experience as a receptionist or previous supervisory experience;
• Has knowledge of the entire Front Office department;
• Is visible in the operation, provides recognition, and fosters positive guest relationships;
• Leads and drives the achievement of various Front Office objectives;
• Has knowledge of the PMS system, OPERA / OPERA Cloud, or similar systems;
• Is outgoing and has excellent communication skills when interacting with guests;
• Is fluent in English (any additional language is a plus!).

We offer you:

Of course you are not alone! An ambitious team is waiting for you that will welcome you with open arms. With us, you benefit from the various benefits of working at Accor! You can count on;

• A gross salary of € 2,863.55 per month based on a 38-hour work week (the salary offered by us is 7,5% higher than the Horeca CAO scale 6);
• Excellent travel allowance from 5.0 km onwards;
• 25 vacation days based on a full-time (38-hour) working week;
• You are invited to stay in Novotel Amsterdam City to a guest experience with a person of your choosing. This includes breakfast and a 3-course dinner meal!;
• Discount for stays at all Accor hotels worldwide;
• Free parking in our hotel;
• Complimentary usage of our Technogym fitness area.

Excited to join?

Are you excited to join Novotel Amsterdam City? Then we would love to meet you! Please, send your CV and motivation letter to Lars, HR Coördinator, via h0515-HR3@accor.com or call us at +31 (0)20 43136 83.

